! The same oxygen chain in a cell quadrupled along z, with each atom's moment
! turned 90 degrees from the one before: the supercell the spiral at
! spiral_q = (0, 0, 1/4) must reproduce. Noncollinear, four species so that each
! atom can be given its own angle2, and no symmetry.
!
! **The k-grid is shifted, and that is not a detail** -- see the header of
! h-chain-90deg.in, which explains it for the norm-conserving case; the reason
! is the same here and has nothing to do with the augmentation charge.
!
! This is the sharpest of the augmented identities: both sides are noncollinear
! ultrasoft (or PAW), so the only thing that differs is whether the transverse
! augmentation charge is carried by the displaced table or by a supercell, and
! q = b3/4 is not its own negative -- which is what makes it, unlike q = b3/2,
! sensitive to the *sign* of the displacement.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.73333333333333,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 4,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) =   0.0
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) =  90.0
    starting_magnetization(3) = 0.6, angle1(3) = 90.0, angle2(3) = 180.0
    starting_magnetization(4) = 0.6, angle1(4) = 90.0, angle2(4) = 270.0
    nbnd = 40
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 O1  16.0  O.pz-kjpaw.UPF
 O2  16.0  O.pz-kjpaw.UPF
 O3  16.0  O.pz-kjpaw.UPF
 O4  16.0  O.pz-kjpaw.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 O1 0.0 0.0 0.00
 O2 0.0 0.0 0.25
 O3 0.0 0.0 0.50
 O4 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 1 0 0 1
